e,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/google-labs-jules%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/google-labs-jules%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/google-labs-jules%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/deangilmoreremix/smartcrmdash/commits/495f550c6a2d7603b5d128bdd9a54ff0c854d271/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-10-30T02:24:30Z","email":"161369871+google-labs-jules[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"google-labs-jules[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-10-30T02:24:30Z","email":"161369871+google-labs-jules[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"google-labs-jules[bot]"},"message":"fix(deploy): correct vite alias configuration for netlify\n\nThe application was failing to deploy to Netlify because of an issue with path alias resolution in the Vite configuration. The alias for `@` was not correctly resolved in the case-sensitive Linux environment used by Netlify.\n\nThis commit fixes the issue by updating the `vite.config.ts` file to use Node''s `path.resolve` to create absolute paths for the aliases. This ensures that the aliases are resolved correctly, regardless of the environment.","tree":{"sha":"8cbc1d494726be362dcc0aba3d30a5fcc92a136c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/deangilmoreremix/smartcrmdash/git/trees/8cbc1d494726be362dcc0aba3d30a5fcc92a136c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/deangilmoreremix/smartcrmdash/git/commits/495f550c6a2d7603b5d128bdd9a54ff0c854d271","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/842251?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/google-labs-jules%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/google-labs-jules%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/google-labs-jules%5Bbot%5D/following