":"https://api.github.com/users/olivio-git/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivio-git/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivio-git","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/StackOverlords/TPS_INTERMOTORS/commits/2a819cd96b0a9fa69f38e8e5d439d0899d896180/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T09:32:31Z","email":"subelzaolivitocabezas@gmail.com","name":"olivio-git"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T09:43:07Z","email":"subelzaolivitocabezas@gmail.com","name":"olivio-git"},"message":"fix(plugins): alinear la URL de los bundles con la ruta real del backend\n\nEl adapter construia `/plugins/<entry>`, pero el backend sirve los bundles bajo\n`/api/v1/plugin-assets/{id}/{path}` (ver rhleone/api-commerce#15). Con la URL\nvieja, Module Federation habria pedido un 404 al cargar cualquier plugin.\n\nLos assets van bajo /plugin-assets/ y no bajo /plugins/ para no mezclarse con\nel CRUD: ese endpoint acepta barras en el path final porque MF pide el\nremoteEntry.js y despues sus chunks con rutas relativas de profundidad\narbitraria.\n\nLa URL se arma sobre environment.apiUrl en vez de una constante hardcodeada.\nSirviendo el SPA desde el public/ del backend eso es relativo (/api/v1), asi\nque plugins y app comparten origen y no interviene CORS.","tree":{"sha":"ce51d312002f857432a6b1df3aaeac5bc663ed23","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/StackOverlords/TPS_INTERMOTORS/git/trees/ce51d312002f857432a6b1df3aaeac5bc663ed23"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/StackOverlords/TPS_INTERMOTORS/git/commits/2a819cd96b0a9fa69f38e8e5d439d0899d896180","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67205387?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivio-git/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivio-git/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivio-git/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivio-git/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/olivio-git","id":67205387,"login":"olivio-git","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3MjA1Mzg3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivio-git/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivio-git/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivio-git/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivio-git/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivio-git/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivio-git","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/StackOverlords/TPS_INTERMOTORS/commit/2a819cd96b0a9fa69f38e8e5d439d0899d896180","node_id":"C_kwDOPFR1DNoAKDJhODE5Y2Q5NmIwYTlmYTY5ZjM4ZThlNWQ0MzlkMDg5OWQ4OTYxODA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/StackOverlords/TPS_INTERMOTORS/commit/a9888ae7a0e8d4d165982fe1f21169d4f9432ffb","sha":"a9888ae7a0e8d4d165982fe1f21169d4f9432ffb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/StackOverlords/TPS_INTERMOTORS/commits/a9888ae7a0e8d4d165982fe1f21169d4f9432ffb"}],"sha":"2a819cd96b0a9fa69f38e8e5d439d0899d896180","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/StackOverlords/TPS_INTERMOTORS/commits/2a819cd96b0a9fa69f38e8e5d439d0899d896180"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67205387?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivio-git/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivio-git/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivio-git/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivio-git/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/olivio-git","id":67205387,"login":"olivio-git","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3MjA1Mzg3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivio-git/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivio-git/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivio-git/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivio-git/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivio-git/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivio-git","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/StackOverlords/TPS_INTERMOTORS/commits/a9888ae7a0e8d4d165982fe1f21169d4f9432ffb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T04:35:46Z","email":"subelzaolivitocabezas@gmail.com","name":"olivio-git"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T09:43:07Z","email":"subelzaolivitocabezas@gmail.com","name":"olivio-git"},"message":"feat(plugins): fuente de plugins para el target web\n\nEl sistema de plugins ya funcionaba en escritorio. Este cambio lo hace andar\ntambien en el navegador, sin tocar el kernel.\n\nQUE YA ERA AGNOSTICO\n\nEl pipeline completo es puro navegador y no necesito ningun cambio:\n\n  PluginSource.list() -> registerRemotes -> loadRemote -> PluginManager\n\nModule Federation carga un bundle remoto por URL en runtime; funciona igual en\nun WebView que en Chrome. Asi que plugin-manager.ts, route-registry.ts,\nloadExternalPlugins.ts, PluginDialogHost y PluginKeybindingHost quedan intactos.\n\nQUE ESTABA ATADO A TAURI\n\nSolo TauriPluginSource, tal como declara su propio comentario. Dos cosas:\nel CRUD via invoke() a comandos Rust, y la construccion de la URL del entry con\nel custom scheme plugin://.\n\nEN WEB ES MAS SIMPLE\n\nToda la maquinaria del custom scheme (handler en Rust, encodeo por segmento,\nvariante para Windows) existe solo para esquivar la restriccion de Tauri para\nservir archivos del disco al WebView. En el navegador el backend expone los\nbundles por HTTP y una URL relativa alcanza:\n\n  plugin://localhost/<id>/remoteEntry.js   escritorio\n  /plugins/<id>/remoteEntry.js             web\n\nSirviendo el SPA desde el public/ del backend, plugins y app comparten origen y\nno interviene CORS.\n\nLO QUE SE AGREGA\n\n- sources/HttpPluginSource.ts: los mismos 4 metodos contra endpoints del\n  backend, usando el cliente axios de la app (hereda token, refresh y formateo\n  de errores). El backend devuelve la MISMA forma que Rust —entry como path\n  relativo, no URL— para que el mapeo a URL viva de un solo lado en cada target.\n- sources/index.ts: getPluginSource() resuelve por target. Los dos puntos que\n  instanciaban TauriPluginSource a mano (main.tsx y PluginSettings) ahora lo\n  piden ahi.\n\nLa deteccion va por @/utils/environment y no por @/platform porque esta rama\nnacio antes de la capa de puertos. Al rebasar sobre development ese helper ya\ndelega en platform/env, asi que no hay nada que migrar.\n\nDIFERENCIA DE MODELO, NO SOLO DE TRANSPORTE\n\nEn escritorio cada usuario instala plugins en SU maquina. En web la instalacion\nes del lado del servidor, asi que los plugins pasan a ser por tenant y\nadministrados centralmente. Es una decision de producto que conviene hacer\nexplicita antes de exponer la UI de instalacion en web.\n\ntypecheck 146, identico al baseline de la rama. eslint sin hallazgos nuevos.","tree":{"sha":"ea72e45a3753752725f87632003af1441d36ee69","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/StackOverlords/TPS_INTERMOTORS/git/trees/ea72e45a3753752725f87632003af1441d36ee69"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/StackOverlords/TPS_INTERMOTORS/git/commits/a9888ae7a0e8d4d165982fe1f21169d4f9432ffb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67205387?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivio-git/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivio-git/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivio-git/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivio-git/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/olivio-git","id":67205387,"login":"olivio-git","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3MjA1Mzg3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivio-git/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivio-git/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivio-git/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivio-git/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivio-git/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivio-git","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/StackOverlords/TPS_INTERMOTORS/commit/a9888ae7a0e8d4d165982fe1f21169d4f9432ffb","node_id":"C_kwDOPFR1DNoAKGE5ODg4YWU3YTBlOGQ0ZDE2NTk4MmZlMWYyMTE2OWQ0Zjk0MzJmZmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/StackOverlords/TPS_INTERMOTORS/commit/e4044b262941afbf48a23005744e669efc2e920f","sha":"e4044b262941afbf48a23005744e669efc2e920f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/StackOverlords/TPS_INTERMOTORS/commits/e4044b262941afbf48a23005744e669efc2e920f"}],"sha":"a9888ae7a0e8d4d165982fe1f21169d4f9432ffb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/StackOverlords/TPS_INTERMOTORS/commits/a9888ae7a0e8d4d165982fe1f21169d4f9432ffb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67205387?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivio-git/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivio-git/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivio-git/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivio-git/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/olivio-git","id":67205387,"login":"olivio-git","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3MjA1Mzg3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivio-git/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivio-git/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivio-git/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivio-git/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivio-git/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/olivio-git","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/StackOverlords/TPS_INTERMOTORS/commits/e4044b262941afbf48a23005744e669efc2e920f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T09:39:46Z","email":"subelzaolivitocabezas@gmail.com","name":"olivio-git"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T09:39:46Z","email":"subelzaolivitocabezas@gmail.com","name":"olivio-git"},"message":"fix(plugins): migrar el storage de plugins al puerto de plataforma\n\nEl rebase sobre development destapo una rotura real: plugin-manager importaba\n`@/stores/tauriPluginAdapterStore`, que la capa de puertos renombro a\n`platformStateStorage`. Los DOS builds fallaban con \"Could not load\".\n\ncreateTauriStorage -> createPlatformStorage. El nombre ademas dejo de mentir:\nen el target web ese storage no tiene nada de Tauri, es localStorage.\n\nDe paso se corrigio el TODO del clear(): el StateStorage de zustand no expone\nclear(), pero el puerto de clave/valor SI (KeyValueStore.clear()), asi que la\nvia limpia es usar getKeyValueStore().open(...) directo en vez de pasar por el\npuente de zustand. El comentario ahora dice eso en vez de apuntar a un\ncreateTauriStorage que ya no existe.\n\ntypecheck 128 (development esta en 126; los 2 de diferencia son propios de esta\nrama). Ambos builds OK. 71/71 tests.","tree":{"sha":"89936698974849a4152723e1bf67d48f95a07814","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/StackOverlords/TPS_INTERMOTORS/git/trees/89936698974849a4152723e1bf67d48f95a07814"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/StackOverlords/TPS_INTERMOTORS/git/commits/e4044b262941afbf48a23005744e669efc2e920f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67205387?v=4","events_url":